  "id": "diethylpropion",
  "term": "diethylpropion",
  "definition": "Diethylpropion is a stimulant drug related to amphetamines that reduces appetite and is used for anti-obesity effects. It acts by increasing catecholamine activity, especially dopamine and norepinephrine, which helps suppress hunger and may also influence brain signals involved in food intake and body weight regulation.",
